<title>POLAND: Commerzbank ups stake in BRE.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank ups stake in BRE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank has increased its stake in Poland's Bank Rozwoju Exportu SA (BRE) to 29 percent from 24.6 percent by buying 640,000 shares, BRE said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said it bought the shares on Wednesday but gave no other details. Last month the Polish central bank cleared Commerzbank to raise its stake in BRE to 32.9 percent and since then the bank has already upped its stake from a previous 21 percent.</p>
<p>Commerzbank, has said it seeks to raise its stake by buying up existing shares rather than taking new share issues.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
